1
00:06:32,307 --> 00:06:38,307
Our lives are the sum of our choices.

2
00:13:04,615 --> 00:13:10,615
Mission: Impossible - The Final Reckoning is a action, thriller,
adventure film directed by Christopher McQuarrie.

3
00:19:36,923 --> 00:19:42,923
Ethan Hunt and team continue their search for the terrifying AI known as the Entity — which has infiltrated intelligence
networks all over the globe — with the world's governments and a mysterious ghost from Hunt's past on their trail.

4
00:26:09,230 --> 00:26:15,230
Joined by new allies and armed with the means to shut the Entity down for good, Hunt is in a
race against time to prevent the world as we know it from changing forever.

5
00:32:41,538 --> 00:32:47,538
Ethan Hunt, played by Tom Cruise.

6
00:39:13,846 --> 00:39:19,846
Grace, played by Hayley Atwell.

7
00:45:46,153 --> 00:45:52,153
Luther Stickell, played by Ving Rhames.

8
00:52:18,461 --> 00:52:24,461
Benji Dunn, played by Simon Pegg.

9
00:58:50,769 --> 00:58:56,769
Gabriel, played by Esai Morales.

10
01:05:23,076 --> 01:05:29,076
Paris, played by Pom Klementieff.

11
01:11:55,384 --> 01:12:01,384
Mission: Impossible – The Final Reckoning is a 2025 American action spy film directed by
Christopher McQuarrie from a screenplay he co-wrote with Erik Jendresen.

12
01:18:27,692 --> 01:18:33,692
It is the direct sequel to Mission: Impossible – Dead Reckoning Part One (2023)
and the eighth installment in the Mission: Impossible film series.

13
01:25:00,000 --> 01:25:06,000
The ensemble cast includes Tom Cruise (in his final portrayal of Ethan Hunt), Hayley
Atwell, Ving Rhames, Simon Pegg, Henry Czerny and Angela Bassett.

14
01:31:32,307 --> 01:31:38,307
In the film, Hunt and his IMF team continue their mission to prevent the Entity, a
rogue artificial intelligence, from destroying all of humanity.

15
01:38:04,615 --> 01:38:10,615
In January 2019, Cruise announced that the seventh and eighth Mission: Impossible films
would be shot back-to-back with McQuarrie co-writing and directing both films.

16
01:44:36,923 --> 01:44:42,923
Plans for the eighth film changed in February 2021, with returning and new cast and crew members being announced soon after, including
Lorne Balfe, who composed the score for two other films in the series; Balfe was later replaced by Max Aruj and Alfie Godfrey.

17
01:51:09,230 --> 01:51:15,230
Principal photography began in March 2022 but was suspended
in July 2023 due to the SAG-AFTRA strike.

18
01:57:41,538 --> 01:57:47,538
Production resumed in March 2024 and concluded in November, with filming
locations including England, Malta, South Africa, and Norway.

19
02:04:13,846 --> 02:04:19,846
Originally subtitled Dead Reckoning Part Two, the film
changed its subtitle in November 2024.

20
02:10:46,153 --> 02:10:52,153
With a $300–400 million budget, The Final Reckoning is
one of the most expensive films ever made.

21
02:17:18,461 --> 02:17:24,461
The Final Reckoning had its world premiere in Tokyo on May 5, 2025, was screened out of competition at the 78th Cannes
Film Festival on May 14, and was theatrically released in the United States on May 23 by Paramount Pictures.

22
02:23:50,769 --> 02:23:56,769
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and grossed $598.8 million
worldwide, while also having the largest opening weekend of the franchise.

23
02:30:23,076 --> 02:30:29,076
It was the last film co-produced by Paramount and Skydance as
separate entities before they merged on August 7, 2025.

24
02:36:55,384 --> 02:37:01,384
The film explores themes of mask, artificial
intelligence (a.i.), diving, submarine, espionage.

25
02:43:27,692 --> 02:43:33,692
The tone is intense.
